  "asr_text": "Some people may choose their words or feel differently when they think they are talking to AI than when they know they are talking to a person. Even if the request is handled without a problem, that does not mean the disclosure issue can be brushed aside with it all worked out in the end. That was exactly the point Meta itself admitted it had got wrong. Convenience matters, but for some people, knowing who they are talking to matters just as much. If AI hands the baton to a person, that one line saying so is part of the service, too. The person taking over does not have to be a secret guest.",
